  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="70d72ee9-4d39-5109-be8b-a4683e470393" activityNameId="7f8009ff-13e3-5f91-a3ce-5aae879dec42" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Inductor, low value multilayer chip type, LMCI, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Inductor, low value multilayer chip type, LMCI, at plant
The data represent a typical low value multilayer chip type inductor, used in the information and communication technology. Material data are taken from datasheets of producers of such inductors. Infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents 1 kg of inductors with a weight of 2.1 miligram/unit. No major updates were made in 2023 - according to recent product sheets from manufacturers, the composition of inductors remains similar. Production efforts dataset is update in a separate module. It is assumed that only global primary metals are used in the inventory.; UUID: 58f0b9ea-bfb8-3c2a-a314-b070a22d8711
This dataset covers raw material input and production efforts for the production of currently used low value multilayer chip type inductors.
Location: Data represent a global valuable composition of low value multilayer chip type inductors.
Technology: average production comprising the following steps: core mounting; epxoy-curing; winding; welding; molding; marking; bending; testing and final control.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: literature
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_58f0b9ea-bfb8-3c2a-a314-b070a22d8711.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
